    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "Yes, the `status` changed like this:\r\n`initial` -> `waiting` -> (button click) -> `initial` (which shouldn't be) -> `finished`.\r\n\r\nIt's supposed to be like this:\r\n`initial` -> `waiting` -> (button click) -> `finished`.\r\n\r\nNow with these commits, after recognition started, if user clicks the button (which triggers `stop`),\r\nthe `stop()` will call `dispose()` and `resetState('finished');`.\r\n\r\n`dispose()` will simply stop the recognition and remove all the event listeners. Now that the listeners are gone, `onEnd` will not be called.\r\nand `resetState('finished')` will set the `status` to `'finished'`.\r\n\r\nTo sum up, in this version, after `(button click)`, `setState` is called only once.\r\nDoes this sound clear to you?",
    "commit_id": "1d97ff99f64bb94f69aa93756f5953f8ed320a4f",
    "created_at": "2019-06-10T14:10:33Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -191,4 +191,19 @@ describe('VoiceSearchHelper', () => {\n     voiceSearchHelper.dispose();\n     expect(stop).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);\n   });\n+\n+  it('stops and the status becomes `finished`', () => {\n+    window.SpeechRecognition = createFakeSpeechRecognition();\n+    const onQueryChange = (): void => {};\n+    const onStateChange = (): void => {};\n+    const voiceSearchHelper = createVoiceSearchHelper({\n+      searchAsYouSpeak: true,\n+      onQueryChange,\n+      onStateChange,\n+    });\n+\n+    voiceSearchHelper.toggleListening();\n+    voiceSearchHelper.toggleListening();",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch/pull/3845#discussion_r292026881",
    "id": 292026881,
