    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "The advantage of the union type is that it completely disappears at runtime, [it's not the case with an enum](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play/index.html#src=enum%20EStatus%20%7B%0D%0A%20%20INITIAL%20%3D%20'initial'%2C%0D%0A%20%20ASKING_PERMISSION%20%3D%20'askingPermission'%2C%0D%0A%20%20WAITING%20%3D%20'waiting'%2C%0D%0A%20%20RECOGNIZING%20%3D%20'recognizing'%2C%0D%0A%20%20FINISHED%20%3D%20'finished'%2C%0D%0A%20%20ERROR%20%3D%20'error'%2C%0D%0A%7D%0D%0A%0D%0Aconst%20eValue%3A%20EStatus%20%3D%20EStatus.INITIAL%3B%0D%0A%0D%0A%2F**%0D%0A%20*%20---%0D%0A%20*%2F%0D%0A%0D%0Atype%20TStatus%20%3D%0D%0A%20%20%7C%20'initial'%0D%0A%20%20%7C%20'askingPermission'%0D%0A%20%20%7C%20'waiting'%0D%0A%20%20%7C%20'recognizing'%0D%0A%20%20%7C%20'finished'%0D%0A%20%20%7C%20'error'%3B%0D%0A%0D%0Aconst%20tValue%3A%20TStatus%20%3D%20'initial'%3B%20). We do have a kind of repetition with the enum too. We duplicate the different values but the compiler helps us with this if the type changes or we do a typo an error is thrown. One advantage of the enum is to be able to enumerate all the possibles values at runtime. But we don't use the feature.",
    "commit_id": "1d97ff99f64bb94f69aa93756f5953f8ed320a4f",
    "created_at": "2019-06-13T10:12:02Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -1,21 +1,32 @@\n-const STATUS_INITIAL = 'initial';\n-const STATUS_ASKING_PERMISSION = 'askingPermission';\n-const STATUS_WAITING = 'waiting';\n-const STATUS_RECOGNIZING = 'recognizing';\n-const STATUS_FINISHED = 'finished';\n-const STATUS_ERROR = 'error';\n-\n export type VoiceSearchHelperParams = {\n   searchAsYouSpeak: boolean;\n   onQueryChange: (query: string) => void;\n   onStateChange: () => void;\n };\n \n+export type Status =\n+  | 'initial'\n+  | 'askingPermission'\n+  | 'waiting'\n+  | 'recognizing'\n+  | 'finished'\n+  | 'error';",
